@baseUrl = https://api.tuodominio.it
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...  # incolla il JWT dopo il login
@userId = 65f8e2c4b3a1d4e8f7a9b0c1  # claim "nameid" dal JWT (decodifica su jwt.io)
@patientId = 65f8e2c4b3a1d4e8f7a9b0c1  # stesso di userId, alias per leggibilità

### ==========================================
### AUTH — api/auth (AuthorizationController)
### ==========================================

### 1. Login (pubblico) — restituisce JWT
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "tuo_username",
  "password": "tua_password"
}

### 2. Validazione token (richiede Bearer) — GET api/auth
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Refresh token — POST api/auth/refresh (richiede cookie refresh_token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh

### 4. Genera hash password (richiede secret "92Pollo92") — POST api/auth/generatehash
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/generatehash
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "tuo_username",
  "password": "nuova_password",
  "hashPassword": "92Pollo92"
}

### 5. Forgot password — POST api/auth/forgot-password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "tuo_username"
}

### 6. Reset password — POST api/auth/reset-password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "token_da_email_hex_64_chars",
  "newPassword": "nuova_password_sicura"
}

### ==========================================
### BLOOD PRESSURE — api/bloodpressure (BloodPressureController)
### Tutti richiedono Bearer token
### ==========================================

### 7. Lista misurazioni per paziente — GET api/bloodpressure/{patientId}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bloodpressure/{{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Crea nuova misurazione — POST api/bloodpressure
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bloodpressure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systolic": 120,
  "diastolic": 80,
  "pulse": 72,
  "timestamp": "2026-10-20T10:30:00Z",
  "context": "Mattina",
  "device": "Omron M7",
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}"
}

### ==========================================
### PATIENTS — api/patients (PatientsController)
### Tutti richiedono Bearer token
### ==========================================

### 9. Lista tutti i pazienti (solo ADMIN) — GET api/patients
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Paziente per ID — GET api/patients/{id}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/{{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Paziente per username — GET api/patients/username/{username}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/username/tuo_username
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Crea paziente (solo ADMIN) — POST api/patients
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mario",
  "surname": "Rossi",
  "birthDate": "1980-05-15T00:00:00Z",
  "gender": "M",
  "weight": 75,
  "height": 178,
  "username": "mario.rossi",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": 1,
  "email": "mario@example.com"
}

### 13. Aggiorna paziente — PUT api/patients
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{patientId}}",
  "name": "Mario",
  "surname": "Rossi",
  "birthDate": "1980-05-15T00:00:00Z",
  "gender": "M",
  "weight": 76,
  "height": 178,
  "username": "mario.rossi",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": 1,
  "email": "mario@example.com"
}

### ==========================================
### PUSH NOTIFICATIONS — api/push (PushNotificationController)
### Tutti richiedono Bearer token
### ==========================================

### 14. Iscrivi a push notifications — POST api/push/subscribe
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/push/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint": "https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/...",
  "keys": {
    "p256dh": "BASE64_P256DH_KEY",
    "auth": "BASE64_AUTH_KEY"
  }
}

### 15. Invia reminder terapia (test) — POST api/push/send/{therapyId}
# AllowAnonymous in dev, ma richiede patientId nel body se non autenticato
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/push/send/therapy-123
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "therapyId": "therapy-123",
  "therapyName": "Ramipril",
  "dosage": "5mg",
  "title": "Promemoria Terapia",
  "body": "È ora di prendere: Ramipril - 5mg",
  "tag": "therapy-therapy-123",
  "url": "/therapies"
}

### ==========================================
### WEATHER FORECAST — api/weatherforecast (WeatherForecastController)
### Swagger/endpoint di default .NET
### ==========================================

### 16. Weather forecast — GET api/weatherforecast
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/weatherforecast

---

### NOTE RAPIDE
- `{{userId}}` / `{{patientId}}` = claim `nameid` (o `sub`) del JWT. Decodifica il token su https://jwt.io dopo il login.
- Il token va incollato in `@token = ...` dopo aver eseguito **Login (1)**.
- Per **refresh token (3)** serve il cookie `refresh_token` (HttpOnly) — REST Client non lo manda automaticamente; usa browser o imposta manualmente `Cookie: refresh_token=...` nell'header.
- `generatehash (4)` richiede l'hardcoded secret `92Pollo92` — solo per setup iniziale password.
- Ruoli: `ADMIN = 0`, `USER = 1` (vedi `Role.cs` in BloodPressureAppLibrary).